Fix opentenbase_ctl install failures observed on real HCE 2.0/aarch64 (issue #73):

1. Fixed-name temp files (./postgresql.conf.user, ./recovery.conf) written
   into the working directory get wedged by leftovers from earlier runs
   (e.g. one created via sudo): every later install by a normal user then
   dies at "Failed to open ./postgresql.conf.user for writing" before
   anything else happens, and the failure paths never cleaned the file up.
   Switch to per-node temp names and always remove them after transfer.

2. check_port_available() ran `ss -tln | grep -q '<port>'` over SSH and
   treated "output empty" as available / "output non-empty" as occupied.
   grep -q never prints, so the result was empty in BOTH cases and the
   decision actually hinged on stderr leaking into the captured output:
   a stale known_hosts entry (host key changed after VM rebuild) made all
   100 port checks fail with "Failed to find available port pair" even on
   a machine with only one listening socket. Inspect the listening table
   itself, discard stderr, and force exit 0 so only a transport failure
   is an error.
